---
import { DAEMON_COMMANDS, SITE } from "../lib/site"
import CodeBlock from "./CodeBlock.astro"
import Section from "./Section.astro"

const BULLETS = [
  "Plain Markdown files with no hidden database: usable in a text editor, in Obsidian and in Git",
  "The daemon binds to 127.0.0.1 only and makes no outbound requests",
  "Host several vaults in one daemon; each one is its own source",
  "Save the current tab from the popup, or search the vault from the address bar",
]

const BODY = "text-base/7 text-pretty text-muted-foreground sm:text-sm/6"
const BUTTON =
  "inline-flex h-11 items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-border bg-card px-4 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-muted focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
---

<Section index="03" title="Your bookmarks as Markdown you own" id="vaults">
  <div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p class={BODY}>
        An optional local daemon turns a folder of Markdown files into a
        bookmark source. Same dashboard, backed by files on your own disk that
        you can read, edit and back up with the tools you already use.
      </p>
      <ul role="list" class="mt-6 space-y-3">
        {
          BULLETS.map((bullet) => (
            <li class:list={["flex items-start gap-3", BODY]}>
              <svg
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke-width="2"
                class="mt-1 size-4 shrink-0 stroke-primary"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" />
              </svg>
              <span>{bullet}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/daemon/" class={BUTTON}>How Markdown vaults work</a>
        <a href={SITE.daemonDocs} class={BUTTON}>Install guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0 space-y-4">
      {
        DAEMON_COMMANDS.map((command) => (
          <CodeBlock label={command.label} code={command.code} />
        ))
      }
      <p class={BODY}>
        All three install the same checksum-verified release. The daemon is
        optional: the extension works without it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
